id: pm-rlm-8xxq
title: Re-run the recursive vs truncated evaluation with a capable local model and a budget that reaches child calls
description: "pm-rlm#23 shipped the evaluation harness (24 versioned questions on two public tracker copies) and an honest first run. That run used functiongemma:270m: both arms scored 0/24 and every recursive run hit its budget before any child call, so it measured the harness, not recursion. Re-run with the strongest local model the host fits (nimble:9b or clef-flash:9b) and a recursive budget that reaches children, while host CPU pressure is low. Also fix the review's non-blocking note: interrupted recursive arms record children: 0 instead of unknown (src/evaluation.ts:58)."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 2
tags[3]: evaluation,local-model,rlm
created_at: "2026-10-25T11:30:31.971Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-26T08:25:44.119Z"
author: claude-hub
acceptance_criteria: "Same capable local model in both arms; at least one recursive run reaches child calls; accuracy, tokens, calls and wall time reported per arm; interrupted arms report children as unknown with a regression test; results recorded on this item.; Run pm rlm eval with a local 9B model only when measured host CPU pressure is below 50 percent; Declare a recursive budget sufficient to reach child calls and record child-call reach with the same model in both arms"
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T08:25:37.750Z",codex-agent,"Reused after searching 9B and the open Task list: this task already covers the requested evaluation follow-up. Owner requirement is now explicit: wait for measured CPU pressure below 50 percent, use a local 9B model in both pm rlm eval arms, declare a recursive budget that reaches children, and report accuracy, tokens, calls and wall time. Preserve the existing interrupted-child-count regression and honest refusal reporting. This sweep only refines planning; no model run or owner decision is claimed. Parent evaluation item pm-rlm-umh4 remains open."
